      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings feel like a heavy, heavy weight to carry all alone, and it is completely understandable why the idea of struggle feeling endless would lead you to question the entire point of continuing.\n\nPlease know that the \"work hard, get better\" narratives can feel dismissive when the pain is so immediate and real, and your philosophical questioning is a brave way of trying to find truth.\n\nWhile the pain of depression is so heavy it can feel like life only hurts, your struggle to find meaning is the first step in trying to build a life that isn't just about enduring.\n\nI hope you can consider that a doctor or therapist might be able to help you understand the \"why\" behind why your brain is feeling this way.\n\nIf these thoughts are becoming too heavy to carry alone, please reach out to a crisis support line.\n\n**If you are in crisis, please call or text 988** (in the US, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year, no matter where you are).",
